# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: load-pathname-relative-under-l -- -l binds *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* to the path as typed, not the absolute path
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-22

* Symptom

Found while documenting *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* (clautolisp 2.3.26).
=(load ...)= and the init files bind it to the ABSOLUTE path of the file
(builtins-core =api.lisp=, "Bind *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* to the ABSOLUTE
pathname"), but a =-l= / positional file binds the string as typed:

#+begin_example
$ cd dir && clautolisp --no-init -l main.lsp
;; in main.lsp: *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* => "main.lsp"
$ clautolisp --no-init -x '(load "dir/main.lsp")'
;; in main.lsp: *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* => "/.../dir/main.lsp"
#+end_example

So the idiom that loads a file beside the current one breaks under =-l=
with a relative path:

#+begin_src autolisp
(load (strcat (vl-filename-directory *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME*) "/helpers.lsp"))
;; -l main.lsp => (vl-filename-directory "main.lsp") is "" => loads "/helpers.lsp"
#+end_src

* Cause

The toplevel driver binds the variable itself around the =-l= action
(=tools/clautolisp/source/main.lisp=, =call-with-dynamic-transmit-binding=
with =(namestring path)=), with the path as parsed from the command line.
alfe's =:direct= mode binds it in the same way (=backend-clautolisp.lisp=);
not checked whether it resolves the path first.

* To do

1. Failing test: =-l REL.lsp= binds the absolute path, as =load= does.
2. Bind the resolved absolute pathname in the clautolisp driver and in alfe's
   =:direct= backend (or let the =-l= action go through the same binding as
   =load=).
3. Remove the caveat from the user manual, section /Image-introspection
   variables/, which points at this issue.

* Fix (2026-10-22, clautolisp 2.3.27 / alfe 2.3.27) -- DONE

The -l / positional action now binds *AUTOLISP-LOAD-PATHNAME* to
(truename FILE) -- falling back to (merge-pathnames FILE) -- exactly as
builtin LOAD does: tools/clautolisp/source/main.lisp
EVAL-ACTION-IN-CONTEXT, and alfe's :direct backend
(backend-clautolisp.lisp, the (:LOAD ...) action) likewise.

Test: transmit-tests.lisp LOAD-PATHNAME-UNDER-L-IS-ABSOLUTE runs the -l
action on "main.lsp" from its own directory and checks the recorded value
is absolute and names the file. Seen red against 2.3.26 (got "main.lsp"),
green now. The user manual's caveat (Image-introspection variables) is
removed. Pure clautolisp: no vendor behaviour involved (the CADs' native
LOAD is not this code path).
